        <description>&lt;img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1637762046888-1e0ab956a31b?ixid=M3w0NjAwMjJ8MHwxfHJhbmRvbXx8fHx8fHx8fDE3ODQyODAwOTR8&amp;ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Featured image of post openinterpreter" /&gt;&lt;h1 id=&#34;openinterpreteropeninterpreter&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/openinterpreter/openinterpreter&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;openinterpreter/openinterpreter&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;Open Interpreter&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;A coding agent optimized for low-cost models. &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/blog/open-interpreter?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=hero_text&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blog post ↗&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;b&gt;English&lt;/b&gt; • &lt;a href=&#34;README_ES.md&#34;&gt;Español&lt;/a&gt; • &lt;a href=&#34;README_ZH.md&#34;&gt;简体中文&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://discord.gg/Hvz9Axh84z&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;Discord&#34; src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/discord/1146610656779440188?style=flat-square&amp;label=Discord&#34; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=docs_badge&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;Documentation&#34; src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/Documentation-white?style=flat-square&#34; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;LICENSE&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;License&#34; src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/badge/License-Apache--2.0-white?style=flat-square&#34; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!NOTE]
&lt;strong&gt;Today: Kimi K3 is here.&lt;/strong&gt; We have reimplemented the provider-recommended
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.kimi.com/coding/en&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Kimi Code&lt;/a&gt; harness in Rust, giving you
maximum K3 performance with a Codex-like interface.
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/kimi-k3?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=kimi_k3_note&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kimi Docs →&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/blog/open-interpreter?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=hero_image&#34;&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&#34;Open Interpreter running in a terminal&#34; src=&#34;https://openinterpreter.com/blog/open-interpreter/blog-hero-1.jpg&#34; width=&#34;100%&#34; /&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;installation&#34;&gt;Installation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;macOS and Linux:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;curl -fsSL https://www.openinterpreter.com/install &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Windows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-powershell&#34; data-lang=&#34;powershell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;irm &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;https&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;err&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;//&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;www&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;py&#34;&gt;openinterpreter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;install&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;py&#34;&gt;ps1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;iex
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then type &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;interpreter&lt;/code&gt; in your terminal to start a session.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;harness-emulation&#34;&gt;Harness Emulation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open Interpreter is a fork of OpenAI&amp;rsquo;s Codex, with a focus on emulating the agent harness that gets the best performance out of low-cost models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;/harness&lt;/code&gt; to switch the active harness:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;12
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&amp;gt; /harness
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;native
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;claude-code
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;claude-code-bare
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;zcode
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kimi-code
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;kimi-cli
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;qwen-code
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deepseek-tui
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;swe-agent
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;minimal
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Read more in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/harness?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=harness_docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;harness docs&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/providers?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=provider_guides&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;provider setup guides&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;acp-compatible-codex-compatible&#34;&gt;ACP compatible, Codex compatible
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open Interpreter works in &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://agentclientprotocol.com/get-started/clients&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ACP-compatible editors and clients&lt;/a&gt;. Configure the client to launch &lt;code&gt;interpreter acp&lt;/code&gt;; see the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/acp&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ACP guide&lt;/a&gt; for examples.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Already building with OpenAI&amp;rsquo;s Codex SDK? Keep the SDK and make a one-line
binary override:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-diff&#34; data-lang=&#34;diff&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;gd&#34;&gt;-const codex = new Codex();
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;gi&#34;&gt;+const codex = new Codex({ codexPathOverride: &amp;#34;interpreter&amp;#34; });
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open Interpreter speaks the same Codex exec protocol. See the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/sdk&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;SDK guide&lt;/a&gt; and run &lt;code&gt;scripts/test-codex-sdk-compat.sh&lt;/code&gt; for a local, provider-free compatibility check.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;computer-use&#34;&gt;Computer Use
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open Interpreter ships with a QA skill that lets any model operate and test interfaces. It can drive web apps in a real browser with &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;agent-browser&lt;/a&gt;, or operate and test native apps with &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/trycua/cua&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;trycua&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;features&#34;&gt;Features
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runs commands inside native sandboxing on macOS, Linux, and Windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switches providers and models from the TUI with &lt;code&gt;/model&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspects or switches Rust-native model harnesses with &lt;code&gt;/harness&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tests web and native apps through the built-in QA skill.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runs as an &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://agentclientprotocol.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Agent Client Protocol&lt;/a&gt; agent for editors with &lt;code&gt;interpreter acp&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeps config and session state local under &lt;code&gt;~/.openinterpreter&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports &lt;code&gt;exec&lt;/code&gt;, MCP, skills, hooks, permissions, and &lt;code&gt;AGENTS.md&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;documentation&#34;&gt;Documentation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=terminal_docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Terminal docs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/quickstart?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=quickstart&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Quickstart&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/install?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=install_guide&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Install guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/config?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=configuration&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Configuration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/cli-reference?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=cli_reference&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;CLI reference&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/harness?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=harnesses&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Harnesses&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/providers?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=provider_guides&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Model provider guides&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/kimi-k3?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=kimi_k3_docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Kimi K3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/deepseek?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=deepseek_docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;DeepSeek&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/zai-glm?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=zai_glm_docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Z.AI, GLM, and ZCode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/acp&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Agent Client Protocol&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/sdk&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Codex SDK&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/sandbox?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=sandbox_approvals&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Sandbox &amp;amp; approvals&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provider and model membership is generated, not maintained as Rust lists. From
&lt;code&gt;codex-rs&lt;/code&gt;, refresh all hosted providers with
&lt;code&gt;python3 scripts/write_provider_catalog.py&lt;/code&gt;, or repeat
&lt;code&gt;--provider &amp;lt;provider-id&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; to update only selected provider entries. Live model
sources require the provider credentials documented in the
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openinterpreter.com/docs/terminal/providers?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=readme&amp;amp;utm_content=provider_catalog_generation&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;provider docs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!NOTE]
This is the new Rust version of Open Interpreter, based on Codex. Looking for the original Python project? It lives on as a community-maintained fork at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/endolith/open-interpreter&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;endolith/open-interpreter&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
